#: docs/specifications/domain/design.md
msgid "How contexts map onto the platform"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/design.md
msgid "**Each context has one steward.** A context owns the catalogs of its resources, listed in the table above, and one role is its steward."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/design.md
msgid "**A product sits inside one context.** Its repository, operational database and tenant entry all belong to that context. If a product needs another context's data, it uses that context's published interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/design.md
msgid "**Contexts connect only through published interfaces.** Those are registry interfaces, domain events, and gold tables with their semantic-layer definitions. No product reads another context's operational database ([CAP-INTEROPERABILITY.8]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/design.md
msgid "**The vocabulary follows the boundary.** A term means what its context's `CONTEXT.md` says it means. Where two contexts use the same word differently, each defines it for itself, and the translation happens at the interface between them."
msgstr ""
